<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1326018" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
A/F Sensor and HO2S On-Vehicle Inspection
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1326018001" page = "2">
<title>
Sensor Heater
</title>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Remove intercooler outlet hose No.2. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1426005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Disconnect A/F sensor and/or HO2S connector with ignition “OFF”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Using ohmmeter, measure resistance of A/F sensor (sensor side) and/or HO2S (sensor side) of sensor heater between terminals “1” and “2” at sensor connector.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, replace A/F sensor and/or HO2S. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1326020"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Temperature of sensor affects resistance largely. Check that sensor heater is at correct temperature.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<spec>
<title>
Sensor heater resistance
</title>
<ptxt>
A/F sensor: 2.8 to 4.5 &#937; at 20 &#176;C (68 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
HO2S: 5.4 to 7.3 &#937; at 20 &#176;C (68 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
